SUMMARY:SkyFest Big Bear — Friday
LOCATION:Multiple venues: Convention Center\, Discovery Center & Snow Summi
 t — Big Bear Lake\, CA 92315
DESCRIPTION:Day one of Big Bear’s dark-sky festival: NASA/Caltech science
 \, an immersive AstroDome\, a free family DiscoverFest\, mountaintop teles
 copes and night hikes\, plus separately ticketed sound-bath and astrophoto
 graphy experiences.\n\nWHEN\nFri\, Aug 14\, 2026\, 12:00 PM–11:00 PM\n\n
 PRICE / ADMISSION\n• Friday 1-day SkyFest pass: $70 and sold out when ch
 ecked August 9\n• AstroFestival-only: $50\; Stargaze-only: $50 and sold 
 out for Friday\n• Child age 12 and under: $15 with a full-price adult\; 
 excludes sound bath and workshop\n• Nighttime DiscoverFest: free\n• Fo
 rest Sound Bath: $40\; Friday astrophotography workshop: $40 and sold out\
 n\nSCHEDULE\n• 12:00–4:00 PM — AstroFestival & Expo at Big Bear Lake
  Convention Center\, 42900 Big Bear Blvd\n• 1:00 PM — Caltech research
 er Cameron Hummels: The Science of Black Holes\n• 2:00 PM — NASA scien
 tist Dominic Benford: Expanding Our View with the Nancy Grace Roman Space 
 Telescope\n• 5:00–8:00 PM — free Nighttime DiscoverFest at Big Bear 
 Discovery Center\, 40971 North Shore Dr\, with family nature walks and noc
 turnal-wildlife learning\n• 6:30–8:00 PM — separately ticketed Fores
 t Sound Bath at Snow Summit\n• 8:00–11:00 PM — Stargaze at the Summi
 t at Snow Summit\, 880 Summit Blvd: Sky Chair\, telescopes\, guided night 
 hikes\, night-sky talks and live painting\n• 8:30–10:30 PM — beginne
 r/intro astrophotography workshop\; separately ticketed and sold out when 
 checked\n\nWHAT TO EXPECT\n• SkyFest celebrates astronomy and dark-sky c
 onservation across three venues\n• A festival pass covers AstroFestival 
 and Stargaze at the Summit\, not the sound bath or astrophotography worksh
 op\n• The 3-day pass was $99 and sold out when checked\n\nUSEFUL NOTES\n
 • Tickets and reservations are activity- and date-specific\; check live 
 availability before going\n• No authoritative event-specific parking or 
 accessibility instructions were found on the current event and ticket page
 s\n\nTBD / VERIFY BEFORE GOING\n• The ticket page describes DiscoverFest
  as 4:00–9:00 PM and appears to imply all three days\; the more detailed
  official program says Friday/Saturday only\, 5:00–8:00 PM. This calenda
 r uses the detailed program\n\nCONFLICTS / SAME-DAY OPTIONS\n• Overlaps 
 or competes with: Skyline at Sundown — Mountaintop BBQ + Live Music (Fri
 \, Aug 14\, 2026\, 4:30 PM–7:30 PM).\n\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\n• Official d
 etailed program: https://www.bigbear.com/events/skyfest/\n• Live tickets
  and availability: https://visitbigbear.ticketspice.com/skyfest-big-bear\n
 \nCALENDAR STATUS: DETAILS_TBD\nLast checked: 2026-08-09\nDetails can chan
 ge. Recheck the official source before making a special trip.
URL:https://www.bigbear.com/events/skyfest/
CATEGORIES:Astronomy,Festival,Family,Outdoors,TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-BIGBEAR-DETAIL-STATUS:DETAILS_TBD
END:VEVENT
