SUMMARY:SkyFest Big Bear — Saturday
LOCATION:Multiple venues: Convention Center\, Discovery Center & Snow Summi
 t — Big Bear Lake\, CA 92315
DESCRIPTION:SkyFest’s fullest day pairs dark-sky and astrobiology talks w
 ith the AstroDome\, free family wildlife programming\, mountaintop telesco
 pes and live painting\, plus separately ticketed mindfulness and photograp
 hy sessions.\n\nWHEN\nSat\, Aug 15\, 2026\, 12:00 PM–11:00 PM\n\nPRICE /
  ADMISSION\n• SOLD OUT — the official page now states that all 2026 Sk
 yFest tickets are sold out\; no Saturday pass\, add-on or workshop remains
  purchasable\n• Nighttime DiscoverFest: free and needs no ticket — thi
 s is the only Saturday SkyFest programming still open to walk-ups\n• For
  reference\, pre-sellout prices were: 1-day pass $70\, AstroFestival-only 
 $50\, Stargaze-only $50\, child 12 and under $15 with a full-price adult\,
  Forest Sound Bath $40\, astrophotography workshop $40\n\nSCHEDULE\n• 9:
 00 AM — Conquer the Wall begins separately at Snow Summit\n• 12:00–4
 :00 PM — AstroFestival & Expo at Big Bear Lake Convention Center\, 42900
  Big Bear Blvd\n• 1:00 PM — Michael Rymer of DarkSky International: Da
 rk Skies — Our Relationship and Responsibility to the Stars\n• 2:00 PM
  — astrophysicist Brandon Holloman: Is Anybody Out There? The Search for
  Life Beyond Earth\n• 5:00–8:00 PM — free Nighttime DiscoverFest at 
 Big Bear Discovery Center\, 40971 North Shore Dr\n• 6:30–8:00 PM — s
 eparately ticketed Forest Sound Bath at Snow Summit\n• 8:00–11:00 PM 
 — Stargaze at the Summit: Sky Chair\, telescopes\, guided night hikes\, 
 night-sky talks and live painting\n• 8:30–10:30 PM — intermediate/ad
 vanced astrophotography workshop\; separately ticketed\n\nWHAT TO EXPECT\n
 • A festival pass covered AstroFestival and Stargaze at the Summit\, not
  the sound bath or astrophotography workshop\n• Without a pass\, the fre
 e 5:00–8:00 PM Nighttime DiscoverFest at the Discovery Center is still w
 orth the trip: family nature walks and nocturnal-wildlife programming unde
 r the same dark sky\n\nUSEFUL NOTES\n• Ticketed SkyFest is closed for 20
 26\; go to the free DiscoverFest instead\, or drive to a dark pullout alon
 g North Shore Drive and stargaze for nothing\n• No authoritative event-s
 pecific parking or accessibility instructions were found on the current ev
 ent and ticket pages\n\nTBD / VERIFY BEFORE GOING\n• The ticket page des
 cribes DiscoverFest as 4:00–9:00 PM and appears to imply all three days\
 ; the detailed program says Friday/Saturday only\, 5:00–8:00 PM. This ca
 lendar uses the detailed program\n\nCONFLICTS / SAME-DAY OPTIONS\n• Over
 laps or competes with: Conquer the Wall — Uphill Race (Sat\, Aug 15\, 20
 26 at 9:00 AM).\n• Overlaps or competes with: Skyline at Sundown — Mou
 ntaintop BBQ + Live Music (Sat\, Aug 15\, 2026\, 4:30 PM–7:30 PM).\n• 
 Overlaps or competes with: Fawnskin Doo Dah Parade — 50th Anniversary (S
 at\, Aug 15\, 2026\, 10:00 AM–3:00 PM).\n• Overlaps or competes with: 
 The Travelin' Band (CCR Tribute) at The Cave (Sat\, Aug 15\, 2026\, 8:00 P
 M–10:00 PM).\n• Overlaps or competes with: Creating Worlds Playwright 
 Festival — Saturday Night (Sat\, Aug 15\, 2026\, 7:30 PM–9:30 PM).\n\n
 OFFICIAL SOURCES\n• Official detailed program: https://www.bigbear.com/e
 vents/skyfest/\n• Live tickets and availability: https://visitbigbear.ti
 cketspice.com/skyfest-big-bear\n\nCALENDAR STATUS: DETAILS_TBD\nLast check
 ed: 2026-08-15\nDetails can change. Recheck the official source before mak
 ing a special trip.
